# TURN_INTO — it turns one thing into another: a block in the world, or a thing he carries.
#
# convert (his bag) and change_block (the world) made ONE, because a child does not split "a wand that
# turns stone into gold" by where the stone is. The MODE is derived by make_item from the shape
# (datapack/TurnInto): a machine takes from his inventory, a thrown thing changes the blocks where it
# lands, a held one changes the block he points at if it matches and otherwise works on his inventory —
# never both in one use. So the body is rendered whole by the tool (ACTS, HELPERS): a template cannot
# loop over a list of FROMs or choose its own mode.
#
# What it keeps from both:
#   - convert's ONE OPERATION: `clear` reports how many it took, so the test and the take are one
#     command and cannot disagree; and it REFUSES OUT LOUD — "You need … in your inventory to use this!"
#     — because a machine that does nothing reads as a broken machine.
#   - change_block's filter: only blocks matching FROM change, and any_block is the curated
#     #moddingfromamod:changeable — never a chest, bedrock or a portal.
#
# ITS OWN COUNTER: declared here, not only by the machine shape's reset, so a held one works in a
# world where no machine was ever made. Adding an objective that exists is harmless.
reset
    /scoreboard objectives add mfam_conv dummy
end

function effect()
${ACTS}
end
${HELPERS}
